<title>USA: IPO FILING -- Introgen Therapeutics Inc.</title>
<headline>IPO FILING -- Introgen Therapeutics Inc.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name		 Introgen Therapeutics Inc</p>
<p>Nasdaq Stock symbol</p>
<p>Estimated price range	   N/A</p>
<p>Total shares to be offered    3.2 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by company	 3.2 million</p>
<p>Shrs outstanding after ipo    10,863,769</p>
<p>Lead Underwriter    Painewebber Inc</p>
<p>Underwriters over-allotment  480,000 shrs  </p>
<p>Business: develops gene therapy products to treat cancer by direct introduction of the therapeutic gene inside the body. Use of Proceeds: To fund product research and development, product clinical trials, manufacturing scale-up and capacity research programs, marketing and sales organization development and other general corporate purposes. Financial Data in 000s, year ended June 30</p>
<p>				   1996		 1995</p>
<p>   - Revenue		 $10,449		$2,664</p>
<p>   - Net Income (loss)   $(1,332)	    ($1,225)</p>
<p>Note: Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc, a party to a collaborative arrangment with Introgen, has agreed to purchase $6 million of the common shares at an assumed initial public offering price of $11 per share.</p>
</text>
